 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 513229,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Solve the system by graphing:\n<br>\n<span data-math=\"\\left\\{ {\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n  y \\geq 3x - 2 \\hfill \\\\\n  y <  - 1 \\hfill \\\\ \n\\end{array}} \\right.\">\\left\\{ {\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n  y \\geq 3x - 2 \\hfill \\\\\n  y &lt;  - 1 \\hfill \\\\ \n\\end{array}} \\right.</span>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"y \\ge 3x - 2\"></span></p>\n<p>Graph the first line as a solid line using the intercept <span data-math=\"\\left( {0, - 2} \\right)\"></span>and the slope of <span data-math=\"3\"></span>.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Test (0, 0).</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"0 \\ge 3\\left( 0 \\right) - 2\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"0 \\ge  - 2\"></span></td>\n<td>This is true. Shade lightly the side where (0, 0) is located.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"y <  - 1\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Graph the second line as a dotted line using the intercept <span data-math=\"\\left( {0, - 1} \\right)\"></span>and the slope of <span data-math=\"0\"></span>. (It is a horizontal line).</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Test (0, 0).</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"0 <  - 1\"></span></td>\n<td>This is not true. Shade lightly the side where (0, 0) is not located.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The solution is the region shaded by both graphs.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "The solution is the lighter shaded region.<br>\n<img src=\"https://exercises.openstax.org/rails/active_storage/blobs/proxy/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsibWVzc2FnZSI6IkJBaHBBcmNLIiwiZXhwIjpudWxsLCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--d99468306e14234d07a018241ef1800f81c8ad2b/CS_Figure_05_10_008.jpg\" alt=\"Two lines are plotted on a coordinate plane. The horizontal and vertical axes range from negative 10 to 10, in increments of 1. The first (dashed) line is horizontal and it passes through y equals negative 1. The region below the line is shaded in gray. The second (solid) line passes through the points, (negative 2, negative 8), (0, negative 2), and (3, 7). The region to the left of the line is shaded in dark blue. The two lines intersect approximately at (0.5, 1). The region below the intersection point and within the lines is shaded in light blue.\">"
    }
   ],
